      "id": 6886,
      "status": "Reported",
      "type": "Technical",
      "section": "A. 4.",
      "date": "2022-03-16",
      "orig": " <rpc message-id=\"601\" xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0\">\n   <establish-subscription\n     xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-subscribed-notifications\">\n     <stream>NETCONF</stream>\n     <stream-xpath-filter xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-vrrp\">\n       /vrrp-protocol-error-event[\n          vrrp:protocol-error-reason=\"vrrp:checksum-error\"]\n     </stream-xpath-filter>\n   </establish-subscription>\n </rpc>",
      "correct": " <rpc message-id=\"601\" xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0\">\n   <establish-subscription\n     xmlns=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-subscribed-notifications\">\n     <stream>NETCONF</stream>\n     <stream-xpath-filter xmlns:vrrp=\"urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:yang:ietf-vrrp\">\n       /vrrp:vrrp-protocol-error-event[\n          derived-from-or-self(vrrp:protocol-error-reason, \"vrrp:checksum-error\")]\n     </stream-xpath-filter>\n   </establish-subscription>\n </rpc>",
      "notes": "The original example put <stream-xpath-filter> element in a wrong namespace, never defined a namespace binding for prefix \"vrrp\" and checked a value of type identityref by treating it as an XPath string literal (instead of using the XPath function from RFC 7950, which is allowed by type definition of leaf \"stream-xpath-filter\")."
    }
  ]
